SUMMARY:The Night Turkey (1973)
LOCATION:Academy Theater\, 7818 SE Stark St\, Portland OR
GEO:45.5191;-122.5829
DESCRIPTION:Dir. William Malone · 52 min\n\nSpoof of the TV Movie 'Kolchak
 : The Night Stalker"\, shot in 1972 by Director William Malone ("House on 
 Haunted Hill"\, "Creature") and his friends\, on a budget of around  $100\
 , in their spare time. It's loaded with people who would later go on to ha
 ve major careers in Hollywood (some eventual Academy Award Winners!). It s
 tars Robert Short later to become an award winning SFX artist  ("Beetlejui
 ce"\, "Splash"\, "Close Encounters Of The Third Kind") as Karl Kornchek an
 d features a stalking Were-Turkey created by master SFX makeup artist and 
 Academy Award winner Rick Baker (who also appears as the dorky date of Tur
 key victim 'Kathy')...\n\nTickets: https://booking.academytheaterpdx.com/l
 aunch/ticketing/cb2e32ec-e607-5133-90e2-13caddc30792\n\nMore showtimes: ht
 tps://mattlohkamp.github.io/small-screens-pdx/
URL:https://booking.academytheaterpdx.com/launch/ticketing/cb2e32ec-e607-51
 33-90e2-13caddc30792
